ormative but the winner of this round  will be whichever film's music makes my  heart soar believe in true love and hope  that peace will reign over conflict well  he was sprightly  especially for a man in heels or i'll  just pick whichever movie's best song my  niece is singing this week the legend  alan menken did the music for tangled  and it was slightly different than some  of his previous efforts films within the  disney empire like hercules as well as  other works featured menken working in  his wheelhouse which would incorporate a  decidedly rock influence style but for  tangled he's been quoted as saying it  was his most pop oriented fun fact the  great tune when will my life begin was  originally going to be a song called  what more could i ever need and was to  feature a much more positive outlook on  being held captive in a tower with some  luxurious amenities and while that may  have suited me just fine i'm the kind of  fellow who could live in a hotel for  years as long as there's a gym netflix  and that fancy lobby water with the  random fruits in it delicious i love it  even more but i get that not everyone is  as simple as me and some people like  rapunzel might want to dream outside of  the confines of their current situation  no amounts of confining could contain  the runaway success of the frozen music  so let's talk about just how great let  it go is i don't  care  what they're going to say  originally elsa was going to be more of  a one note character but the evolution  of this tune helped deepen her own  emotional journey written by robert and  kristen anderson lopez both saw this as  an opportunity to get more than surface  level with elsa kristin thought the song  would be a perfect conduit to describe  the intense pressure and scrutiny that  women go through on so many levels on a  daily basis and robert wanted the number  to reflect the feeling of being a  straight a student then suddenly failing  a test where do you go from here but the  